    "Tobacco avoidance is crucial for the prevention of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD). Individuals are advised to engage in regular physical activity and follow a healthy diet rich in fruits, vegetables, and whole grains, while minimizing trans fats and added sugars. Clinicians are encouraged to work closely with patients to facilitate lifestyle changes, address barriers, and track progress. Social determinants of ASCVD risk should also be considered. Risk estimation should guide the use of pharmacological therapies and coronary artery calcium measurements in intermediate-risk individuals.": [],
